    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d690">

                <pb facs="1253" n="1237" sameAs="frus:frus1950v04/pg1237"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.6121/8–3050: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Douglas</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d690-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                    <lb/><seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-08-30T18:00:00+01:00">August 30, 1950—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1287. UK FonOff informs Embassy they have decided to cease publication of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">British Ally</hi> in Moscow with next issue and public
                    announcement to that effect will be made by HMG within a few days pending which
                    this information remains confidential.</p>
                <p>Main motivation of British is economy since production of magazine in Moscow
                    rather expensive. Circulation practically impossible <pb facs="1254" n="1238"
                        xml:id="pg1238"/> and it no longer earns anything. British would have
                    preferred Soviets to ban it and for that reason put “hot” material in recent
                    issues but without desired effect.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Douglas</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d690-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d690-f1-content">
                <p>The Department relayed this telegram to the Embassy in the Soviet Union at 6:00
                    p. m. on August 30.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
